meta {
  name: Manually retry by resolving the incident (Operate "Retry" equivalent)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{camundaRest}}/incidents/{{incidentKey}}/resolution
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Manual retry, part 2 of 2

  Resolving the incident re-activates the job that `05-reset-job-retries` re-armed —
  together they are the API equivalent of Operate's "Retry" button. Because BIKE-FAIL
  is a *permanent* simulated outage, the job runs, fails again, and the incident
  returns once the fresh retries are exhausted. That is the teaching point: a manual
  retry re-runs the work but is not a fix for a systematic error. To demonstrate an
  actual fix, start a fresh request with a valid bike id (e.g. BIKE-900) and watch it
  complete.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}
